        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Adolfo Bioy Casares, James Norman Hall, Victoria Ocampo, Silvina Ocampo, Charles Nordhoff\n- Roles: fiction writer, journalist, translator, author\n- Works: Mutiny on the Bounty\n\nFacts:\n- James Norman Hall was born on April 22, 1887, and died on July 5, 1951.\n- Adolfo Bioy Casares was born on September 15, 1914, and died on March 8, 1999.\n- James Norman Hall was an American author best known for the novel \"Mutiny on the Bounty,\" which he wrote with Charles Nordhoff.\n- Adolfo Bioy Casares was an Argentine fiction writer, journalist, and translator.\n- Silvina Ocampo was a writer and the sister of Victoria Ocampo.\n- Silvina Ocampo was married to Adolfo Bioy Casares.",
